  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A brief familiar warmup is always included; the conductor has approved its exercises, and willing section leaders can demonstrate them.\", \"decision\": \"Who should guide the shared vocal warmup?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nDifferent section leaders each guide one part of the approved warmup in a posted order. Responsibility is shared across the choir while the fixed sequence keeps the brief preparation coordinated and predictable.\nThe conductor guides the familiar warmup and adjusts the pace after listening to the choir’s responses. The person directing the rehearsal also hears how the group is settling before beginning the planned pieces.\nA section leader guides the approved warmup while the conductor listens from elsewhere in the room. The choir receives a familiar sequence, and the conductor gains a different listening position before detailed rehearsal begins."
    }
  ],
